{
  "reviews": {
    "node-13lt8zz": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims 'No evidence currently establishes whether field valves were open contrary to procedure or if an unrecorded service-routing change occurred.' The supporting source (IA-D01) explicitly states it is a location index and does not establish valve positions. However, the claim treats this lack of information as proof that we cannot determine if valves were opened contrary to procedure. This conflates 'absence of record' with 'evidence of absence'. We do not know if field valves were open; we only know the directory doesn't show them.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A current piping diagram, valve status log, or witness testimony confirming whether specific isolation valves (M-101/M-102) were in their expected position at 10:00 AM.","question":"Does a record exist that shows the physical state of field valves M-101 and M-102 at approximately 10:00 AM on May 20, 2024?"
    },
    "node-10hrgmy": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims 'No evidence currently establishes whether external factors (third-party work, utility outage) affected the supply.' The supporting source is simply a lack of records in the current packet. This does not establish that no third party was working or that an upstream outage did not occur; it only means we haven't seen those logs yet.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Third-party work permits, cross-functional coordination logs for Utilities area on May 20, and site utility distribution system status records covering the time window around 10:00 AM.","question":"Are there third-party work permits or upstream utility outage reports applicable to the RHOB instrument-air supply line between 09:54 and 10:08?"
    },
    "node-11co87q": {
      "supported": true,
      "issue": "",
      "evidenceNeeded": "",
      "question": ""
    }
  },"decision":{
    "summary":"The investigation board contains two unsupported condition nodes that incorrectly treat missing records as proof of absence. Node-13lt8zz and node-10hrgmy must be revised to reflect uncertainty rather than asserting 'no evidence establishes' without qualifying the gap.","evidenceUsed":["b678a928-a8d2-472d-bc03-2e1a3dc411e6#1","fcd254db-75b3-4a9d-abec-44c5b6a9b34e#1"],"unknowns":["Actual valve positions at time of event.","Whether third-party work or upstream outage caused the pressure drop."],"alternatives":["The interruption originated from a local field-valve misposition not captured in records.", "An external utility disturbance occurred without being logged as an internal incident."],
    "confidence":0.95
  }
}
